###< symfony/sendgrid-mailer ###

###> Site Configuration ###
SITE_BASE_SCHEME=http
SITE_BASE_HOST=localhost:8000
###< Site Configuration ###

# Now obviously,
# we don't want to hardcode these -
# at least not the second value:
# it will be different on production.
# Instead, we need to set these as new environment variables.
# And in .env, the SITE_BASE_URL is almost what we need.
# We just need it to be kind of split into two pieces.
# Hmm. Check this out, create two new environment variables:
SITE_BASE_SCHEME=https
SITE_BASE_HOST=localhost:8000